<title>CANADA: Toronto stocks drop at open but avoid Dow's tumble.</title>
<headline>Toronto stocks drop at open but avoid Dow's tumble.</headline>
<text>
<p>CHANGE				  CHANGE</p>
<p>TSE	   6733.12  -33.73   HI 6806.87	LO 6760.37</p>
<p>DJI	   7827.05 -116.14 GOLD (LONDON)   US$323.50 -2.65</p>
<p>FTSE	  4895.90  -95.40 GOLD (COMEX OCT)US$326.80 +0.70</p>
<p>NIKKEI     19326.03 +103.41 LME CASH NICKEL US$6575     -35</p>
<p>CANDLR	 1.3882	   LME CASH ALUM   US$1735   +20.5</p>
<p>CAN 30-YR    118.89   -0.70 BRENT CRUDE     US$18.91  -0.15</p>
<p>-------------------MARKET COMMENT-------------------------</p>
<p>* Toronto stocks lost ground at Friday's open but avoided Wall Street's 100-point tumble. * Double-witching helped create volatility. * 6 million shares traded worth C$90 million.</p>
